# fixedbugs, defect 563, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 204's R2; the
# critic's Expect and libjpeg, whose `expect.h` line 222 and libjpeg's
# `jmorecfg.h` line 175 each define `EXTERN`, one as an object and one as a
# function).
#
# The two headers here do the same with `FIXEDBUGS_563_EXTERN`, each
# whatever came before, so no order of the two groups compiles: this order
# is refused and the other is told refused too, by the one clang run that
# asked it. Until 2026-10-10 either built at exit 0 under a warning. What
# remains is a header of the program's own with an `#undef` between them,
# which the note drafts and the `guess` fixes name.
extern "fixedbugs-563-tcl.h"
    function tcl_level() -> i64

extern "fixedbugs-563-jpeg.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function jpeg_level() -> i64

function main()
    print(tcl_level())
    print(jpeg_level())
